{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{x+3}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\  & ↓ & 4 \\\\  & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{x-4}=1+\\frac{7}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+3}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1+\\frac{7}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-49404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] ["math" "x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $7$ | $4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-7$ |\n|  | $7$ | $-3$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}=7-\\frac{3}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(7-\\frac{3}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7x\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =7(2-0)-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+1|) \\\\  & =14-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =14-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,3\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352216" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-352216" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352216" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352216" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352216" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 \\\\  & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}=2-\\frac{1}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{2x-3}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}(2-\\frac{1}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}2\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{|}_{2}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =2(3-2)-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2-1|) \\\\  & =2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-49353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/re