x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "5x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "5x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "5x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{x+3}=1+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1+\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{-2}^{0}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-2+3|) \\\\  & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "-3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -9 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\  & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49456" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-347423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-347423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $3$ | $8$ | $3$ | $-2$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $2$ |\n|  | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}=3{x}^{2}+2x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+2x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}-x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}-x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{0}^{3}]+[{2}^{2}-{0}^{2}]-[2-0] \\\\  & =8+4-2 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-347423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-347423" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-347423" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,\\,5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}={x}^{2}+x+\\frac{5}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+x+\\frac{5}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}+5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-352251" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352251" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352251" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-352251" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-114879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-114879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 3 & 1 \\\\  & 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}=3x+1+\\frac{2}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3x+1+\\frac{2}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-114879" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-114879" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-114879" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{x}^{2}+x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"] ["math" "3{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"] ["math" "{x}^{2}-2x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-114879" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\  & ↓ & -2 & 10 & -18 \\\\  & 1 & -5 & 9 & -16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}={x}^{2}-5x+9-\\frac{16}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}-5x+9-\\frac{16}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+9\\int \\text{d}x-16\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-49421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+3x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-49421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-114892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-114892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 3 & -4 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & 3 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} & =3-\\frac{(\\frac{17}{2})}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{17}{2x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-17{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[3x-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3(2-0)-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(2)+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(0)+3|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})] \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d