il "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x+3)} & =1+\\frac{(-4)}{(x+3)} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4}{(x+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{4}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\int \\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-73392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8e91c02ba20fbea134c908e328151703f7c74397295a2b0d8d666d753e26a5"} {"question" "q-73392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042267/state.json" "file_sha256" "76d9a54e523855792e179a9597805116dd945a177b4ed6b03a30ef36d5996700"} {"question" "q-73392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}-4\\